  "result": "The rule and its four witnesses for `NRS_484B_223_3c` now pass the gate (`OK`), using 2 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_223_3c.lean`):\n- **Who it applies to:** the subject is a vehicle (`DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`) and also belongs to traffic (`DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic`).\n- **When it applies:** there is a centre turn lane `c` lying on a highway `h`, and the subject has been in `c` at every observation since a left turn (`drv_motion_left_turn`) was recognized while it was in `c`. At some point in the turn window before that, the subject was not on `h`; that is what makes it a turn \"onto the highway\".\n- **The duty:** for every such pair of lane and highway, the distance travelled while that holds is at most 50 ft (written as `Units.feet 50`). The count stops when the subject leaves the centre lane, which is the node's own reading of \"merging\".\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_223_3c.lean`) are built on a three-lane highway with a driveway off it to the south:\n- **forbid:** after the turn, the subject travels 30 m in the centre lane.\n- **permit:** it travels 10 m in the centre lane, then moves to a through lane.\n- **idle:** it drives straight in a through lane.\n- **blind:** the forbid trace with the yaw rate hidden.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **Run 1, `WITNESS_FAIL`:** the gate rejected my turn traces as physically inconsistent. The headings didn't follow from the yaw rates, and one lane-change step's path length was shorter than the distance actually covered. I rebuilt the turn as a single exact 90° step and made path length always cover the distance between scenes.\n2. **Run 2, `OK`.**\n\n**Choices you may want to review:**\n- **Where \"traffic\" goes:** the node claims the traffic aggregate on s1 and s6 but doesn't say what it applies to. I wrote it as \"the subject is part of traffic\" in the applicability.\n- **90° instead of 85°:** the forbid narrative says the turn is 85°, but the witness turns 90° so the headings stay exact. That is still well inside the 45°–135° band that counts as a left turn.\n- **No narrowings:** I declared none of my own.\n\nOne extra command of mine, a `--help` variant of the gate, was blocked because it needed approval this session can't get. It never ran and didn't count toward the budget.\n\nThe full report is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
